      "content": "Yes, that's correct and a widely held argument. highway expansion can indeed create \"induced demand,\" where the added capacity encourages more driving, leading to increased traffic volumes, congestion, and air pollution. This can ultimately render the initial investment in highway expansion ineffective and even counterproductive. By prioritizing high-speed rail and public transit, cities can reduce their reliance on cars, mitigate environmental impacts, and create more sustainable transportation systems.",
